From aa68be11774a064203321c95ffbc1128fb908ae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:18:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wmr: add WMR_HMD_THREAD_NO_RT diagnostic gate (T194/T195)

Env-gated skip of the SCHED_FIFO max-priority request on the WMR read
thread, added to test whether that priority combined with 0049's 10ms
backoff sleep was starving Basalt's own threads via preemption churn.

Tested (T195): disabling it did NOT stop the SLAM pose-rate collapse,
and a real perf sched trace separately showed the thread's own
scheduling delay is negligible (max 0.026ms) -- this rules out the
theory rather than confirming it. Left in place, off by default, as a
cheap diagnostic knob rather than reverted, since it cost nothing to
keep and the question may come up again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
index da3d33d64..894e1b6b1 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
@@ -732,7 +732,12 @@ wmr_run_thread(void *ptr)
 
 #ifdef XRT_OS_LINUX
 	// Try to raise priority of this thread.
-	u_linux_try_to_set_realtime_priority_on_thread(wh->log_level, "WMR: USB-HMD");
+	// T194 experiment: WMR_HMD_THREAD_NO_RT=1 skips this to test whether SCHED_FIFO max
+	// priority combined with 0049's 10ms backoff sleep is what starves Basalt's own
+	// threads (see docs/pruebas.jsonl T194). Temporary, not a real fix either way.
+	if (getenv("WMR_HMD_THREAD_NO_RT") == NULL) {
+		u_linux_try_to_set_realtime_priority_on_thread(wh->log_level, "WMR: USB-HMD");
+	}
 #endif
 
 
